Shipping src/json/build.rs/license/readme retained. Separate examples and integration test targets not vendored. Local changes: bounded transport deadlines, cancellation, worker retirement; connected websocket URL getter; owned startup stderr readiness polling (Unix poll / Windows PeekNamedPipe), shared absolute startup deadline and typed timeout. Process teardown retains synchronous kill/wait ownership: OS reaping and temporary-profile filesystem cleanup are NOT hard-deadline bounded; no detached cleanup or reader worker is created.
Browser target initialization failures now retain discovery instead of retiring the browser event receiver. Failure diagnostics include target/process identity and protocol error code without raw page/protocol data. A disconnected browser event listener is removed without shutting down unrelated CDP response routing. Deterministic fake-CDP regressions cover failed attach, failed Page.enable, later healthy Browser.getVersion and valid-target discovery, disconnected listeners, and explicit waiter/worker cleanup. Existing deadline, cancellation, no-replay and process ownership behavior is unchanged.
Pruned stale upstream documentation examples using obsolete protocol APIs, syntax or attribute-result shapes, and examples asserting against live external websites. The valid fixture-backed find_elements example is retained. Public API prose and remaining examples are retained. Local rustfmt normalization is also applied.
